.TH WB\-STATUS 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-status \- list the issues in the flow and where each stands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR status [<issue>] [\-\-stage <heading>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
List the issues in the flow under headings, as git status lists files: each issue under the last step it has done (Not broken down, Broken down, Accepted, Tested, Built, Reviewed, Fixed), and last the issues that have a question no [answers] or [answer] line has closed.
.PP
An issue is in the flow when its branch, local or at origin, holds a commit that the default branch of origin does not. Git alone says which, and nothing is fetched. Its line shows the branch, the open change as #<n> (change_of_branch) and how many commits are not pushed. The comments come from issue_comments.
.PP
It writes nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B <issue>
Print that issue, in the flow or not, with its title (issue_address) and what it was worked out from.
.TP
.B \-\-stage <heading>
Print that heading only, whatever its case.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every issue could be read.
.TP
.B 1
A pattern failed for one issue. It is listed under Not read.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
